 Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer"],"id":"long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.57 (Commuting prime-power differences)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.57, p. 59, label lem:mixed-prime-power-layer","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For a function $g:\\mathbb N_{>0}\\to\\mathbb Z$, a positive integer $p$ and an integer $e\\ge1$, define\n$$\n(\\Delta_{p,e}g)(n)=g(p^en)-g(p^{e-1}n).\n$$\nThese operators commute. If $p\\ne q$ are primes, $e,f\\ge1$, $A\\subseteq\\mathbb N_{>0}$, $n\\ge1$ and $\\gcd(n,pq)=1$, then\n$$\n(\\Delta_{q,f}\\Delta_{p,e}c_A)(n)\n   =\\sum_{d\\mid n}\\mathbf1_A(p^eq^fd).\n$$\nThus the mixed difference counts precisely the support elements whose $p$- and $q$-adic exponents are $e$ and $f$ in this divisor sum.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.MaximalOmegaLayer.mixedPrimePowerLayerTwo_supportCoeffInt%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-mixed-prime-power-layer%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.MaximalOmegaLayer.mixedPrimePowerLayerTwo_supportCoeffInt%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.MaximalOmegaLayer.mixedPrimePowerLayerTwo_supportCoeffInt"},{"deri